{{Quote|Tehar. Never heard of it. Must be out in the Unknown Regions.|Ello Asty|audio=TeharElloAsty-TheChildrenFromTehar.flac|<ref name="Children">{{Resistance|The Children from Tehar}}</ref>}}
'''Tehar''' was an obscure terrestrial [[planet]] located in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] near the [[Unknown Regions]]. The world was home to a [[human]] population known as the Teharans, and it was the site of a [[Unidentified village (Tehar)|village]] that featured a [[Unidentified temple (Tehar)|temple]] of [[the Force]]. In [[34 ABY]], the planet suffered an [[Attack on Tehar|attack]] from [[First Order]] [[First Order Army|forces]] under the [[Commanding officer|command]] of [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] that completely devastated the world.

Stowing away on a [[Freighter|cargo ship]], the Teharan [[Youngling|children]] [[Eila]] and [[Kel]] consequently became the only survivors, eventually finding themselves on the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]]. While evading subsequent First Order search efforts, the children shared the knowledge of Tehar's destruction with the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and [[Technician|mechanics]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] and [[Neeku Vozo]].

==Description==
{{Quote|I hate this place, Kel. I wanna go back to Tehar.''"<br />"''You know we can't do that, Eila. It's gone. There's nothing there anymore. We're safe here.|Eila and Kel|audio=TeharNothingLeft-TheChildrenFromTehar.flac|<ref name="Children" />}}
Tehar was a terrestrial<ref name="Eila" /> [[planet]]<ref name="USWNE" /> located in the [[Tehar system]]<ref name="Appendix" /> of the [[Mid Rim Territories]]<ref name="AppendixCorr" /> near the [[Unknown Regions]].<ref name="Map">{{StarWarsGalaxyMap}}</ref> It was situated in grid square I-7 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="AppendixCorr" /> After the [[Attack on Tehar]], [[Commanding officer|led]] by<ref name="Eila" /> [[First Order]] leader<ref name="USWNE" /> [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], the planet was reduced to smoldering ash.<ref name="Eila" />

==History==
===Attack on Tehar===
{{Quote|The First Order, they came to our world. Started destroying everything. Our family, our friends&mdash;we escaped before they could get to us.|Eila, to Tamara Ryvora|audio=EilaTehar-TheNewTrooper.flac|<ref name="Trooper">{{Resistance|The New Trooper}}</ref>}}
Tehar was a relatively unknown planet.<ref name="Ace" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="34 ABY">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the [[Attack on Tehar]], as well as the events of ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' and [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]], to [[34 ABY]].</ref> First Order [[First Order military|forces]] led by Ren attacked a [[Unidentified village (Tehar)|village]] on Tehar. The [[Kel and Eila's family|siblings]] [[Eila]] and [[Kel]] were the only survivors, as they escaped on a [[Freighter|cargo ship]] while their [[homeworld]] was devastated.<ref name="Children" /> The [[Youngling|children]] arrived at the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]] on the planet [[Castilon]], where they attempted to hide.<ref name="USWNE" /> When the First Order learned of the existence of the survivors, they placed a [[bounty]] of twenty thousand [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] on the children to ensure any evidence of the massacre on Tehar was liquidated.<ref name="Ace" />

[[File:EilaAndKel-TheChildrenFromTehar.png|thumb|right|255px|Tehar natives Eila and Kel]]
After receiving information on Eila and Kel's location, [[Captain]] [[Phasma]] of the First Order dispatched [[agent]]s&mdash;which included a [[Unidentified tech stormtrooper (Colossus)|tech stormtrooper]] and a standard [[Unidentified First Order stormtrooper (Colossus)|stormtrooper]], with both being led by [[Commander]] [[Pyre]]&mdash;to the ''Colossus'' to [[Hunt for Eila and Kel|locate]] the children. Eila expressed a desire to return to Tehar, only to be reminded by Kel that there was nothing for them to return to. The younglings then met the [[Chelidae]], a native Castilon [[species]] that worked in the ''Colossus''{{'s}} [[Colossus Engineering Level|engineering levels]], who introduced them to [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]]. Eila and Kel explained to Xiono, his [[BB-series astromech droid|droid]] companion [[BB-8]], and his friend [[Neeku Vozo]] that they fled Tehar&mdash;the name of which Xiono did not recognize&mdash;after Ren destroyed their home. Xiono then vowed to assist the children in escaping the First Order.<ref name="Children" />

===Teharans avoiding the First Order===
{{Quote|Mission accomplished. The children are no more.''"<br />"''Excellent. Now the name Tehar will fade from memory.|Pyre and Phasma|audio=MissionAccomplished-TheChildrenFromTehar.flac|<ref name="Children" />}}
[[File:PyreReports-TheChildrenFromTehar.png|thumb|left|250px|Pyre reports the supposed deaths of the last Teharans to Phasma.]]
BB-8, Kel, Xiono, and Vozo subsequently visited the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]] to acquire [[Plant|herbs]] in order to treat Eila's broken [[Limb|leg]]. Phasma's forces spotted Kel and gave chase to the group. After returning to the [[engineer]]ing level, Xiono inquired as to the reason for the First Order's interest in the children, which was not known to Eila. Then, Xiono orchestrated a plan to fake the children's [[death]]s, which the Chelidea helped facilitate. Pyre and<ref name="Children" /> his<ref name="USWNE" /> [[trooper]]s were successfully deceived, and Pyre reported the supposed accomplishment to Phasma. Phasma was pleased by the report, remarking that the name "Tehar" would fade from existence and the actions of the [[First Order Army|First Order]] would be left undiscovered by the Resistance. When Xiono reported the incident to Resistance member [[Ello Asty]], the [[Abednedo]] did not recognize Tehar either and theorized that the planet resided in the Unknown Regions.<ref name="Children" />

After the First Order [[Occupation of the Colossus|occupied]] the ''Colossus'', a [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] designated [[CS-515]] encountered Eila and Kel while the children were [[fishing]] for [[snarlfish]]. After discovering the children did not have an [[Colossus identification badge|identification badge]], CS-515 sought to [[Prison|arrest]] the Teharans. The children resisted and, in the resulting scuffle, knocked the trooper unconscious. The siblings once more sought Xiono's help and led him, BB-8, Vozo, and [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] to CS-515's unconscious body. While the Resistance spy [[Theft of First Order data rod|disguised]] himself as CS-515 to ensure that the stormtrooper had not reported the children's existence to the First Order, Ryvora, too, questioned why the First Order was hunting Eila and Kel, prompting Eila to recount the planet's fate to her&mdash;though, as before, Kel could not name a reason for the First Order's actions.<ref name="Trooper" />

[[File:SectorSet-GalacticStarcruiser.png|thumb|right|225px|Tehar was represented by a space on the Sector Set board.]]
Later in 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="34 ABY" /> Eila and Kel [[Mission to Ashas Ree|traveled]] to the planet [[Ashas Ree]]. While exploring an [[Ashas Ree outpost|outpost]] there, they found a [[Ashas Ree Temple of the Force|temple of the Force]] that reminded Eila of the temple from their village on Tehar. Kel remarked that the structure was larger than the Teharan temple and featured unfamiliar symbols on its exterior.<ref name="Relic">{{Resistance|The Relic Raiders}}</ref> Later still in that same [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="34 ABY" /> Tehar and its system were represented by a space in the [[board game]] [[Sector Set]].<ref name="Halcyon">{{GSAttr|Sector Set}}</ref> Aboard<ref name="Atrium">{{GSAttr|Atrium (Halcyon)}}</ref> the [[Purrgil-class starcruiser|''Purrgil''-class starcruiser]]<ref name="Datapad">{{DatapadCite|Halcyon|Halcyonp1-GSDatapad.png|Halcyonp2-GSDatapad.png}}</ref> ''[[Halcyon]]'', the game was played by a group of passengers in the starcruiser's [[Atrium (Halcyon)|Atrium]].<ref name="Atrium" />

At some point, the Attack on Tehar was documented in the [[First Order Archives]].<ref name="RNF">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="RiseDate">{{RiseAndFallDate}}</ref> [[historian]] [[Beaumont Kin]] referenced Tehar as a victim of the First Order's conquest in<ref name="RNF" /> his<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> [[book]] ''[[The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''.<ref name="RNF" />

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|Tehar?''"<br />"''That's where we're from. Tehar. Our home.|Kazuda Xiono and Kel|audio=TeharOurHome-TheChildrenFromTehar.flac|<ref name="Children" />}}
The planet's population included [[human]]s who were known as Teharans, including the children Eila and Kel.<ref name="USWNE" />

==Locations==
{{Quote|Kel, this place reminds me of our temple back home.''"<br />"''Yeah. But much larger.|Eila and Kel|audio=TeharTemple-TheRelicRaiders.flac|<ref name="Relic" />}}
A village on the planet was the site of a temple of [[the Force]],<ref name="Ace" /> although the attack from the First Order completely devastated the world.<ref name="Trooper" />

==Behind the scenes==
Tehar was first mentioned in "[[The Children from Tehar]],"<ref name="Children" /> the sixth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which aired on [[November 4]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney release">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref>

